# Commit messages

When creating a git commit, write a **detailed** message. Never use one-liners like `wip`, `fix`, `update`, or `misc`.

Required shape (Conventional Commits subject is OK):

1. Subject: imperative, specific, ~50–72 chars (`ci: add GitHub Actions lint/test workflow`)
2. Blank line
3. Body: at least a few sentences or bullet points covering **why**, what a reviewer should know, and any follow-ups

The local hook `.githooks/commit-msg` rejects thin messages. Do not skip it with `--no-verify`.
